# Review decisions on light (Z 1-25) EXFOR capture datasets, in the format of the research repository's
# data/curate/review_decisions.jsonl (the human-decision file of the WP-12 quality model, used for the Z 26-92 decisions).
# scripts/build_light_curation.py appends these lines to that file and passes the result to quality_model.run
# (human_decisions), so each line overrides the automatic decision for its dataset; the data stay in the tables with
# decision "exclude". One JSON object per line: entry, subentry, pointer, decision, reason (with the EXFOR id), reviewer,
# date; superseded_by names the dataset that replaces an excluded one. Every line was checked against the EXFOR entry of
# the 2026-10-14 entry.zip by an agent (reviewer "agent:claude-opus-5.5"); no person has reviewed them yet.
{"entry": "13139", "subentry": "13139008", "pointer": "", "decision": "exclude", "reason": "Ne-22 (n,g) Winters+Macklin 1988 (ApJ 329, 943), EXFOR 13139008: STATUS (CURVE), effective cross sections digitised from Fig. 4-5 only in 17-170 eV windows around six peaks (2.67, 5.29, 22.6, 76.5 keV, ...), with errors mostly larger than the values; the mean of these points over a 0.1-dex energy cell is a peak value, not the cell-averaged cross section (a different quantity: x2400 vs Almeida 21808010), and the authors' own Table 2 MACS 13139006 omits these six peaks.", "reviewer": "agent:claude-opus-5.5", "date": "2026-11-06"}
